  "problem": "Which of the following is a variable?\n\nI. $\\sqrt{z}-1$\n\nII. $z$\n\nIII. $z+y$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's look at each one in turn.\n\nI. $\\sqrt{z}$ is an algebraic expression, not a variable.\n\nII. $z$ is a variable because it's a single letter by itself.\n\nIII. $z+y$ is an algebraic expression, not a variable.\n\nSo, only choice II represents a variable.",
